    "created_at": "2017-07-27T14:34:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-07-27T14:34:48Z",
    "body": "I agree. Perhaps we could say something like this:  If the intrinsic size of the canvas element is equal to the layout size of the canvas element (e.g. if the width and height style properties are set to 'auto', which is the default), then a CSS pixel in the rendering context's coordinate space is equal in size to a CSS pixel in the canvas element's layout coordinate space. Otherwise, the canvas element's content is resized to fit, using the algorithm specified by the 'content-fit' CSS property.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
